 "root_cause": "Source registration and component probing were outside the service task set, and job creation was unowned until its result reached submit. Close could miss the I/O or a subsequently spawned job, while reusing the full timeout again for processor cleanup.",
 "changes": [
  "Own source registration, job creation/result handoff and component probing before their first I/O",
  "Reuse shielded admission so caller cancellation does not discard actual work or automatically retry it",
  "Reject draining admission before any database/network/processor calls",
  "Drain subsequent job tasks created by already admitted submits, not only the initial close snapshot",
  "Share one monotonic close deadline between task drainage and processor reclamation"
 ],
